  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/0dbe5ee12862e19946119f787f6ee246fad46188</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/commit/0dbe5ee12862e19946119f787f6ee246fad46188"/>
    <title>
        fix(cerebras): add Qwen3.8 27B cached-read pricing (#8408)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-30T04:25:42Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143489229?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>Arian-Urdu</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/Arian-Urdu</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix(cerebras): add Qwen3.8 27B cached-read pricing (#8408)

Cerebras bills cached input tokens at the standard input rate, so
cache_read equals input ($0.99 per million tokens). Without cache_read,
consumers cannot tell a missing price from free cached tokens.

Source: https://inference-docs.cerebras.ai/capabilities/prompt-caching#how-are-cached-tokens-priced&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
